  Repaint this grey block mockup as a finished video game screenshot of a market town square. 16-bit SNES pixel art, isometric 2:1 projection, warm earthy palette (browns, tans, terracotta, forest green, stone grey, gold, deep red, sky blue), single dark outline, medium shading, light from the top left, medieval central European, 14th century. Crisp pixels, no blur, no text, no UI. Keep EXACTLY the camera, the position, footprint and height of every building, the streets, the water and the little people: the people are 1.7 m tall adults and set the scale; do not shrink or enlarge any building. The cream blocks become half-timbered town houses of 2 and 3 storeys (plaster, oak beams, jettied upper floors, terracotta and slate roofs, chimneys); the big stone block with slate roof is the town hall with an arcade on the ground floor and a coat of arms; the long grey building with the tower is a gothic parish church; the small red-roofed boxes are market stalls with cloth awnings and goods. Add life: crates, barrels, a fountain, banners, carts, many townsfolk.

